BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR THE MCCLELLAND & STEWART'S AUTHOR SALON
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T220000
UID:bm-5215620260528@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/26_0272_M
 andSSalon_INSTAPOST_1080x1350.jpg?cb=1777649008
DESCRIPTION:[Book Launch]\nJoin McClelland & Stewart on Thursday\, May 28t
 h for their annual Author Salon\, as they celebrate their 120th anniversar
 y. In partnership with TIFA and Flying Books\, the McClelland & Stewart Au
 thor Salon is a gathering in celebration of their authors\, their readers\
 , and their community.\nA scathing and thought-provoking exploration of po
 wer and philanthropy\, Sharon Bala’s GOOD GUYS shows the dark side of ch
 arity\, and what happens when you try to change the world for all the wron
 g reasons.\n\nFearless and vulnerable\, UNSHAMING from Jowita Bydlowska tr
 anscends the typical self-help memoir and challenges the narrative surroun
 ding addiction\, exploring new ways to evolve the conversation.\n\nSet in 
 a near-future Kolkata ravaged by climate change and social disharmony\, Me
 gha Majumdar’s A GUARDIAN AND A THIEF follows five characters as their l
 ives collide in this propulsive and shattering tour de force.\n\nWith expe
 rt storytelling that will leave you high on passion and inspiration\, Mark
  Medley’s LIVE TO SEE THE DAY is a globe-trotting exploration of what dr
 ives certain people to pursue a dream.\n\nAchingly relatable and intensely
  funny\, Amil Niazi’s LIFE AFTER AMBITION looks at how the concept of am
 bition has shaped her and a generation of Millennials.\n\nAnd finally\, fi
 rst published in 1969\, THE EDIBLE WOMAN is Margaret Atwood’s brilliant 
 first novel\, introducing her as a consummate observer of the ironies and 
 absurdities of modern life.\nGET YOUR TICKETS HERE!
LOCATION:Paradise Theatre\, 1006 Bloor St W\, Toronto\,
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR THE LAUNCH OF SILVER LAKE BY ALEX PUGSLEY
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T200000
UID:bm-5232220260601@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/silver_la
 ke_Toronto_launch_poster.png?cb=1778625016
DESCRIPTION:[Book Launch]\nJoin Flying Books and Biblioasis for the launch
  of Alex Pugsley's new novel\nSilver Lake!\nPugsley\, alongside the actors
  David Chinchilla\, Blaise Crocker\, and John Fitzgerald Jay\, will read a
 nd perform scenes from the novel. Books will be available for sale and sig
 ning.\nIt was on a fully dark February night when I went to the Communist'
 s Daughter to meet a friend who never showed that my life in movies began.
 \nSo begins the third installment in a series of standalone novels about t
 he life and travels of Aubrey McKee. Set in Toronto and Silver Lake\, a cr
 eative neighbourhood in Los Angeles\, the novel chronicles with infectious
  élan Aubrey’s journey from broken-hearted derelict to B-movie producti
 on assistant\, comedy writer\, and science-ﬁction screenwriter\, all the
  way up to feature ﬁlm director. Along the way\, he encounters long-ago 
 childhood friends\, manic producers\, NHL players turned talk show hosts\,
  Victoria’s Secret models\, impulsive movie stars . . . and his own risi
 ng destiny.\nAlex Pugsley has worked on over 185 produced episodes of tele
 vision\, writing for performers such as Lauren Ash\, Scott Thompson\, Dan 
 Aykroyd\, and Michael Cera. He wrote and directed the feature ﬁlm Dirty 
 Singles which won for him the Irving Avrich Emerging Filmmaker Award at TI
 FF. Following the publication of his first novel\,\nAubrey McKee\,\nhe was
  named one of CBC’s Writers to Watch. His ﬁrst story collection\,\nShi
 mmer\,\nwas nominated for the ReLit Award for Short Fiction\, and his most
  recent novel\,\nThe Education of Aubrey McKee\,\nwas long listed for the 
 Toronto Book Awards. His next book\,\nThe Hungarian Ballroom\,\nan Aubrey 
 McKee novella\, is forthcoming from Biblioasis. More information can be fo
 und at www.alexpugsley.com.
LOCATION:Flying Books\, 784 College Street
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR AN AUTHOR SOCIAL WITH LARISSA PHAM
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T203000
UID:bm-5216620260603@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/Larissa_P
 ham_w_Marlowe_Author_Social.jpg?cb=1778080948
DESCRIPTION:[Author Social]\nJoin us for a conversation with Larissa Pham 
 author of\nDiscipline\n\, in conversation with Marlowe Granados\, Flying B
 ooks author of\nHappy Hour.\nAdmission is free\, but space is limited. Pl
 ease RSVP to attend.\nDiscipline\nis a taut\, electrifying debut about a 
 woman forced to confront unsettling truths about herself\, her past\, and 
 the life she rebuilt following a ruinous affair with her former mentor\, f
 rom “a writer to keep a close eye on” (\nThe New York Times Book Revie
 w\n)\n\nChristine is on tour for her novel\, a revenge fantasy based on a 
 real-life relationship gone bad with an older professor ten years prior. N
 ow on the road\, Christine is seeking answers—about how to live a good l
 ife and what it means to make art—through intimate conversations with st
 rangers\, past lovers\, and friends.\n\nBut when the antagonist of her nov
 el—her old painting professor—reaches out in a series of sly communiqu
 es after years of silence to tell her he's read her book\, Christine must 
 reckon with what it means to lose the reins of a narrative she wrote preci
 sely to maintain control. When her professor invites her to join him at hi
 s cabin\, deep in the woods of Maine\, what she encounters threatens to ch
 ange the very foundations of her life as she's imagined it.\n\nA delicatel
 y explosive high-wire act about the fictions we construct for ourselves ju
 st to survive\, Discipline is a terse triumph about art-making and rigor\,
  intimacy and attention\, punishment and release.\nLARISSA PHAM\nis the au
 thor of the essay collection\nPop Song\n\, a finalist for the National Boo
 k Critics Circle John Leonard prize. Her writing has appeared in\nGranta\n
 \,\nThe Nation\n\,\nThe New York Times Book Review\n\,\nBookforum\n\, and 
 elsewhere. She holds an MFA in fiction from the Bennington Writing Seminar
 s and teaches at the New School’s MFA in creative writing.\nDiscipline\n
 is her first novel.\nMARLOWE GRANADOS\nis a writer and filmmaker. She coho
 sts The Mean Reds\, a podcast dedicated to women-led films\, and her advic
 e column\, "Designs for Living\," appears in\nThe Baffler\n. After spendin
 g time in New York and London\, Granados currently resides in Toronto.\nHa
 ppy Hour\nis her debut novel.
LOCATION:Flying Books at Neverland\, 371 Queen St. W.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR THE LAUNCH OF NIGHTBERRIES
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T200000
UID:bm-5167220260604@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/Nightberr
 ies_Launch__1_.png?cb=1777570279
DESCRIPTION:[Book Launch]\nFlying Books\, CMU Press and River Street Writi
 ng are delighted to host the launch of\nNightberries\nby Elina Penner in c
 onversation with Sherri Klassen.\nDream or reality\, nightmare or trustwor
 thy memory?\nNightberrie\ns is a dark modern fairytale from German author 
 Elina Penner about the enigma who is Nelli Neufeld. The quiet youngest dau
 ghter in a noisy\, tangled German Mennonite family who fled from Russia in
  the 1990s\, Nelli seems to be coping well in a traditional marriage. But 
 what is going on in her memory? As we follow the events on two key days in
  2020\, we are asked riddles about Nelli that even she might not be able t
 o answer.\nA hauntingly original\, sometimes absurdly comic psychological 
 tale from contemporary Germany\,\nNightberrie\ns has been translated into 
 English by Bradley Schmidt from the 2022 novelNachtbeeren.\nElina Penner w
 as born in 1987 as a Mennonite German in the former Soviet Union and moved
  to Germany in 1991. Plautdietsch (Low German) is her mother tongue. After
  time spent in Berlin and the US\, she now lives with her family in the Ea
 st Westphalia region of Germany. She is a successful personal essayist and
  blogger\, with many of her non-fiction pieces gathered in the 2023 collec
 tion\nMigrantenmutti (Migrant Mother\n).\nNachtbeeren\nwas her first novel
 . In 2025\, her second novel\,\nDie Unbußfertigen (The Unrepentant\n)\, w
 as released in Germany.\nSherri (S.L.) Klassen is the author of\nMenno-Nig
 htcaps: Cocktails Inspired by that Odd Ethno-Religious Group You Keep Mist
 aking for the Amish\, Quakers or Mormons\n(Touchwood\, 2021. She has also 
 published in the\nConrad Grebel Review\nand\nThe Journal of Mennonite Writ
 ing\n. She was long known for her Mennonite-themed blog:\nThe Drunken Menn
 onite\n\, some pieces of which were reprinted in\nThe Anabaptist World Rev
 iew.\nShe has recently started writing on substack and has two novels in p
 rogress. She lives in Toronto and eats zwieback and verenijke from time to
  time\, but never verenijke made with nightberries.
LOCATION:Flying Books\, 784 College St.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ROMANCE IN THE CITY WRITING WORKSHOP
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260608T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260608T203000
UID:bm-5435720260608@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/SPECIAL_G
 UEST.png?cb=1779283484
DESCRIPTION:[Workshop]\nROMANCE IN THE CITY WRITING WORKSHOP WITH LEANNE T
 OSHIKO SIMPSON\nBack by popular demand!  An evening of city romance\, unfo
 rgettable characters\, and slow-burn chemistry.\nStreetcars at dusk\, hidd
 en cafés\, chance encounters\, and summer nights that change everything 
 — Toronto is full of places where love stories begin. Get ready for an  
 interactive writing workshop on building chemistry\, unforgettable charact
 ers\, and city romance. Includes prompts\, discussion\, Q&A\, and a specia
 l guest: Lavanya Lakshmi\, author of the upcoming novel\nLeave and Come Ba
 ck.\nLeanne Toshiko Simpson teaches creative writing and literature\nat th
 e University of Toronto. Her debut novel\,\nNever BeenBetter\n\, was named
  one of CBC’s Best Books of 2024\,\nand was featured on Good Morning Ame
 rica and in\nElle\nCanada\, Toronto Star\,\nand\nThe Seattle Times\n.\nTic
 ket price includes:\n A two-hour writing workshop  A glass of wine (or non
 -alcoholic beverage) to enjoy during the workshop A $20 book credit\, usab
 le for that night only.  Curated list of writing resources from Leanne.\n
 GET YOUR TICKETS HERE!
LOCATION:Flying Books at Neverland\, 371 Queen St. W.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
